# ==============================================================================
# GHC 9.6 Base Package Configuration
# ==============================================================================
#
# Package: ghc9.6-base-redhat
#
# DESCRIPTION:
#   This template manages the base configuration for the Glasgow Haskell Compiler
#   (GHC) version 9.6 on Red Hat-based systems.
#
#   NOTE: The 'ghc9.6-base' RPM package itself does not ship a traditional
#   global text configuration file (like .conf or .ini). It provides the compiler
#   binaries, runtime libraries, and base prelude packages in /usr/lib64/ghc-9.6/.
#
#   Configuration is typically handled via:
#   1. Environment Variables (e.g., GHC_PACKAGE_PATH, TMPDIR)
#   2. Cabal Project Files (cabal.project, cabal.project.local)
#   3. Stack Configuration Files (stack.yaml)
#
#   Since no parametrizable global config directives exist in the default package
#   distribution, this template serves as a documentation anchor and potential
#   placeholder for environment variable exports if needed by dependent roles.
#
#   If you need to configure GHC behavior globally, consider using a drop-in
#   script in /etc/profile.d/ or a systemd drop-in if GHC is run via systemd.
#
# ==============================================================================

# No global configuration file exists for ghc9.6-base.
# Any environment-specific overrides should be handled in the consuming role
# or project-specific configuration files.
